{"name":"Sunset Orange","hex":"#fd5e53","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"sunset orange","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A dark and saturated orange color."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sunset_orange"}],"entries":[{"title":"Blood orange","blocks":[{"text":"The blood orange is a variety of orange with crimson flesh colored near or the same as blood. It is one of the sweet orange varieties. It is also known as the raspberry orange."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5d/BloodOrange.jpg/330px-BloodOrange.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Blood_orange"},{"title":"Sunset (color)","blocks":[{"text":"The color sunset is a pale tint of orange. It is a representation of the average color of clouds when the sunlight from a sunset is reflected from them."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/58/Sunset_2007-1.jpg/330px-Sunset_2007-1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sunset_(color)"},{"title":"Sunset","blocks":[{"text":"Sunset is the disappearance of the Sun at the end of the Sun path, below the horizon of the Earth due to its rotation. As viewed from everywhere on Earth, it is a phenomenon that happens approximately once every 24 hours, except in areas close to the poles. The equinox Sun sets due west at the moment of both the spring and autumn equinoxes. As viewed from the Northern Hemisphere, the Sun sets to the northwest in the spring and summer, and to the southwest in the autumn and winter; these seasons are reversed for the Southern Hemisphere."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f6/Full_cycle_of_a_Sunset_on_the_high_plains_of_the_Mojave_Desert.jpg/330px-Full_cycle_of_a_Sunset_on_the_high_plains_of_the_Mojave_Desert.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sunset"},{"title":"Orange (colour)","blocks":[{"text":"Orange is the colour between yellow and red on the spectrum of visible light. The human eyes perceive orange when observing light with a dominant wavelength between roughly 585 and 620 nanometres. In traditional colour theory, it is a secondary colour of pigments, produced by mixing yellow and red. In the RGB colour model, it is a tertiary colour. It is named after the fruit of the same name."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d8/Delicatearch.png/330px-Delicatearch.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Orange_(colour)"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ec/Immature_Moro_blood_orange_fruit_-_7_months_from_flowering.jpg/500px-Immature_Moro_blood_orange_fruit_-_7_months_from_flowering.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ec/Immature_Moro_blood_orange_fruit_-_7_months_from_flowering.jpg/1280px-Immature_Moro_blood_orange_fruit_-_7_months_from_flowering.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ec/Immature_Moro_blood_orange_fruit_-_7_months_from_flowering.jpg/500px-Immature_Moro_blood_orange_fruit_-_7_months_from_flowering.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Immature 'Moro' blood orange fruit – 7 months from flowering","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AImmature_Moro_blood_orange_fruit_-_7_months_from_flowering.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/15/Bloodorange1.jpg/500px-Bloodorange1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/15/Bloodorange1.jpg/1280px-Bloodorange1.